      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "A <b>doubled consonant</b> after a short prefix (<i>acc-</i>, <i>aff-</i>, <i>coll-</i>, <i>imm-</i>, <i>irr-</i>, <i>supp-</i>) is often the sign of a prefix that changed its last letter. Undo the change to find the prefix: <i>ac-cede</i> is <i>ad-</i> + <i>cede</i>."
      },
