      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Find the hidden prefix",
        "q": "What prefix is hiding in <b>aggregate</b>, and what does the word mean?",
        "steps": [
          "The doubled <b>gg</b> after the first <i>a</i> is the clue: <b>ad-</b> became <b>ag-</b> before the <i>g</i>.",
          "What is left is <b>greg</b> (flock, as in <i>congregate</i>) + <b>-ate</b>.",
          "Put it together: “flocked toward one another,” many things gathered into one group."
        ],
        "a": "ad- (to). An aggregate is a whole formed by combining many parts; a total."
      },
